{
  "challenge": "C-005",
  "task": "Return the greatest common divisor of all input integers as a nonnegative integer.\n\nImplement `int common_divisor(const int *values, size_t count)`. Ignore signs. The result for an empty list or an all-zero list is 0; gcd(0, n) is abs(n). At most 100 integers, each in -10000..10000.\n\n## Examples\n\nInput: `[18, 24, 30]` → output: `6`.\nInput: `[0, -12, 18]` → output: `6`.\n",
  "language": "c",
  "file": "common_divisor.c",
  "starter": "// TODO: implement the task.\n#include <stddef.h>\nint common_divisor(const int *values, size_t count) { return 0; }\n",
  "entrypoint": "common_divisor",
  "adapter": "#include \"mm_json.h\"\n#include <stdlib.h>\nint common_divisor(const int *, size_t);\nmm_value *mm_call(const mm_value *args) {\n    const mm_value *list = mm_at(args, 0);\n    size_t n = mm_length(list);\n    int *a = calloc(n + 1, sizeof(int));\n    int *out = calloc(n + 1, sizeof(int));\n    for (size_t i = 0; i < n; i++)\n        a[i] = (int)mm_integer(mm_at(list, i));\n    return mm_new_integer(common_divisor(a, n));\n}\n",
